# Writer 12 (session 7c, A2). L §5.14 `on d`: "A day that is a hole and not a window has no bound, so that is every
# span, earlier ones included, whatever the instance's `when` says: its booking cut min(t, K) is a hole with it
# (§5.14.3)." L §5.14.3: "An amount, or a `when`, that was a hole at its cut stays a hole movement until a version
# answers it." A keyed decision `g[j in ks]` (`reads acct`) whose day and `at` are the hole hday, at places that keep
# no parts, is a hole movement: the balance it reaches is a hole naming hday, as its plan twin's is (writer 12's
# scratch a2/np_plan.tally, amount wage_amt and no `reads`, prints these three lines). refcore had crashed with
# KeyError: 'j' (triage scratch a2/v23, here without parts: writer 12's a2/np_dec.tally).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
index ks = [a, b]
place acct[j in ks]: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
input hday: date
move w1[x in savings on wage_day]: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to x amount wage_amt
move g[j in ks]: transfers
  on hday
  at hday
  reads acct
  leg cash from acct[j] to world amount bal(acct[j])
ask q: bal(acct[a], 2026-12-31)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[acct[a]] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[acct[b]] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
  hday = ?"not yet"
=== expect
q: ?"not yet" (hday)
  unfulfilled: w1[acct[a]]
  cut 2026-12-31
